Platform: one-socket Xeon 6741P (Granite Rapids-SP, family 6 model 0xAD, 48 cores /
96 threads), the CPU of crescent, the host of the cross-host runs in EXPERIMENTS.md.
Its four Arc Pro B70 GPUs are left out (tests/console/moe/xeon6741p-4xb70 on the
plan-moe-bandwidth branch covers them); this fixture is the CPU side for the on-die
gap list (docs/intel-on-die-accelerators.md section 4).

From the host (read 2026-10-20):
- proc/cpuinfo (first processor block, so the real flags line: amx_tile/int8/bf16,
  avx512_fp16, cat_l3, cat_l2, rdt_a, mba, no amx_fp16) and the 16 SMBIOS type 17
  records (8x 64 GiB DDR5-6400 RDIMM, 8 slots empty), read as root on crescent for
  tests/console/moe/xeon6741p-4xb70 (plan-moe-bandwidth branch); capture.sh keeps the
  formatted area of each record and drops its strings.
- MemTotal/MemFree/MemAvailable, CPU 0's L3 sharing list (0-95), kernel 7.0.0-31.
- From the read-only inventory in docs/intel-on-die-accelerators.md section 5.1
  [L-crescent]: 3 DSA (8086:0b25), 3 IAA (8086:0cfe), 3 QAT 402xx (8086:4944, driver
  4xxx, two sym;asym and one dc, state up, 0 VFs), 3 DLB 2.5 (8086:2714, no driver);
  /dev/isst_interface (isst_tpmi); SDSi bound with a 32-byte state_certificate; TPMI
  PLR present; intel_ifs_0/1 untested with no image; HWP min = max = 3.8 GHz, EPP 0,
  governor performance; four TPMI uncore domains with ELC 0; SNC off (one node);
  resctrl registered but not mounted; zswap/demotion off; no CXL memory device.

ARK (https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/241828/intel-xeon-6741p-processor-288m-cache-2-50-ghz/specifications.html,
read 2026-10-20): 8 memory channels, DDR5 6400 MT/s, no MRDIMM; QAT/DLB/DSA/IAA 3
default devices each; SST-BF 12 high-priority cores at 2.6 GHz, 36 at 2.1 GHz;
SST-TF yes; SST-PP no; base 2.5 GHz, max turbo 3.8 GHz.

Not from hardware (made up, consistent with the above):
- BDFs and root buses, the auxiliary device parent (0000:00:03.1), the SMT numbering
  (siblings +48), per-CPU cache lists, the uncore domains' agent_types (two compute
  dies with core agents, two I/O dies: the inventory reports 4 domains but not their
  agent types), their min/max (800 MHz to 2.2 GHz compute, 2.5 GHz I/O), swap,
  uptime, numa_balancing 1, and every cpufreq base_frequency at 2.5 GHz (SST-BF off:
  the inventory read neither its state nor the high-priority CPUs).
- No /dev/cpu/0/cpuid: its records sit at offset leaf | subleaf << 32, so leaf 7
  subleaf 1 would be a 4 GiB file; tests/detect_test.sh covers the CPUID read with
  sparse files instead (crescent's leaf 24H EBX is 0x70001, AVX10.1).
- intel-speed-select is not on the fixed PATH, so doctor names the node image copy.

Layout: exactly what tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes from a host-shaped tree.
